E = {
    32: "He crawls around, burned across the face by the gas that smells like a sweet odor of something just sickly wrong, something you would never tell anyone about. He mutters out his pain below. His hives strucken across himself, his needle marks countless, where their cause hangs also in the maiden he was locked inside of. He rolls out across the floor onto his back.",
    34: "I remember this moment, my heart sinks and stops. I scream the way I knew how before, all those lifetimes, “Christopher!” I lunge at his body on the ground. He looks blue… He is not breathing. I can’t help. The words escape me, frantic sways in the voice, “No! No!—No!” I say. I find myself saying it through trembles over and over, my hand sitting unstill in the weightless pins and needles. My hand feels cut apart in mixtures of wobbly constants with cold and warmth unalike. Trembling words tell him again, “No! No! No!” The room staggers tall as the small floor shrinks, not real but real, and the reality is the feeling covering the truth behind it, my heart of mine can’t flutter its chokes much longer.",
    43: "My fingers feel big and thuddy, like heavy rounds of wet blubberies. I know I reach the phone because I can see it, even though my flesh makes my head shrink into perceptual confusion. I don’t want to know everything is a not too random thought right now… My hands clam in clammy. Pale steps closer. Flatlining almost; feeling as if. The gun stuffed at me of God’s will forces me; felt in certains forcefully fed. True cruelty: watching compliance unfold as act raped unto you, for a theater disturbed. The phone slides now, soaked from my sweaty and shuddering grasp. The tremolant stutters finger tip points more. Wet quiver quakes of another hand now over top the ringing phone I hold. What now? I breathe in vibrations like my hands and body; the panic drowning the physical.",
    53: "My sight is overwhelmed by my watering eyes, and I see it, the eyelids full with cusps of liquid reveal tears that traveled from cheek. They made it onto his lip. The tiny little movements of salt water find their way over the hump, down the little slide into his mouth. The hill of his upper lip now overcome, where my water is inside of him. His eyes open beneath me, his eyes barely seen through his curling black eyelashes; my Christopher’s soul awaits me behind those eyes. I need to see his soul.",
    57: "“Alice…?” he says to me. He sees me.",
}
